Description: Fix for AIKIDO-2026-310861 (CWE-843 type confusion via thenable
 smuggling during untrusted Promise deserialization in the seroval core).
 .
 The vulnerable logic lives in the `seroval` core package
 (packages/seroval/src/core/context/deserializer.ts), where a deserialized
 Promise fulfillment/rejection value that is itself a thenable is passed
 straight to the deferred resolver, allowing an attacker to smuggle an
 unexpected type past the deserializer. Upstream fixed this in seroval 1.6.2
 by adding an isThennable() guard that throws SerovalMalformedNodeError.
 .
 The `seroval-plugins` package ships NO copy of that source — its published
 tarball contains only package.json, dist/ and web/. It is affected purely
 transitively through its dependency on the vulnerable `seroval` core.
 Upstream's fix commit (f1ffcc9) therefore made no source change in
 seroval-plugins; it only bumped the depended-on `seroval` version to the
 fixed 1.6.2. This patch performs the same remediation against the file the
 seroval-plugins tarball actually distributes: it pins the `seroval`
 dependency to the fixed >=1.6.2 line, so the guarded deserializer is what
 gets installed and executed.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/lxsmnsyc/seroval/commit/f1ffcc96d259f9b5b3d71feb262b58240c90e7b7
--- a/package.json
+++ b/package.json
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
     "@types/node": "^24.10.0",
     "@vitest/ui": "^4.0.6",
     "pridepack": "2.6.4",
-    "seroval": "1.5.2",
+    "seroval": "1.6.2",
     "tslib": "^2.8.1",
     "typescript": "^5.9.3",
     "vitest": "^4.0.6"
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
     "vitest": "^4.0.6"
   },
   "peerDependencies": {
-    "seroval": "^1.0"
+    "seroval": ">=1.6.2"
   },
   "scripts": {
     "prepublishOnly": "pridepack clean && pridepack build",
